{%- comment -%}
  Fire Safety widget: our own card header around the StationWorks
  <burn-status> embed, rendered and kept live by permits.sjifire.org. The embed
  draws in a shadow root, so site.css cannot reach in -- theme it only through
  the --burn-status-* variables in site.css, which also strip its own card
  chrome so it sits flush under our header.
  Config (script, agency id, publishable key) lives in site.json burn_widget.
  The key is a publishable pk_live_ key: it identifies the site, grants nothing.

  The embed's button goes to the portal and only shows while a permit is on
  sale; all year its "More information" link points at our Burn Information
  page. That link is left off the Burn Information page itself.
  more-info-href must be absolute. The production URL is rendered, then the
  inline script swaps in this page's own origin so previews and local dev link
  to their own copy. The widget reads the attribute once, when its script
  (later in the page, never preloaded) defines the element, so the swap always
  lands first.

  Once the script loads, the widget handles its own API failures. The fallback
  notice covers the cases it can't: the script itself failing to load (portal
  down, content blocker) via onerror, and JavaScript off via <noscript>.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign burn_info_path = '/services/burn-permits/' -%}
{%- capture burn_fallback -%}
  &#9888; Live fire status unavailable. Call
  <a href="tel:+13603785334">(360) 378-5334</a>
  or see
  <a href="{{ site.permits_url }}">Burn Permits &rsaquo;</a>
{%- endcapture -%}
<section class="widget widget--burn-status" aria-labelledby="fire-safety-title">
  <div class="widget__header">
    <div class="flex">
      <svg aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href='#flame' /></svg>
      <div>
        <h2 class="widget__title" id="fire-safety-title">Fire Safety</h2>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <burn-status
    agency-id="{{ site.burn_widget.agency_id }}"
    key="{{ site.burn_widget.key }}"
    layout="compact"
    button="when-on-sale"
    {%- if page.url != burn_info_path %}
    more-info-href="{{ site.prodUrl }}{{ burn_info_path }}"
    {%- endif %}
  ></burn-status>
  {%- if page.url != burn_info_path %}
  <script>
    document.currentScript.previousElementSibling.setAttribute(
      "more-info-href",
      location.origin + "{{ burn_info_path }}"
    );
  </script>
  {%- endif %}
  <p class="widget__notice" data-burn-fallback hidden>{{ burn_fallback }}</p>
  <noscript>
    <p class="widget__notice">{{ burn_fallback }}</p>
  </noscript>
</section>
<script
  async
  src="{{ site.burn_widget.script }}"
  onerror="document.querySelectorAll('[data-burn-fallback]').forEach(function (el) { el.hidden = false; })"
></script>
